*testing* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

Testing with Combine

*Usage:*

- ''chippy combine test''                     Run the project's test suite
- ''chippy combine test <file>''              Run the tests in one test file
- ''chippy combine test <pattern>''           Run the tests whose names match a pattern
- ''chippy combine test <file> <pattern>''    Run the matching tests in one test file
- ''chippy combine <config> test ...''        Any of the above with an explicit combine config file

The ''<file>'' slot is interpreted as a test file only when it contains ''/'' or ends with ''.chp''. Everything else is interpreted as a pattern.

*Configuration:*

This only honours the options ''Project'', ''Version'', ''Paths'' and ''External'', as nothing is written to disk.

*Test files:*

- Must be named with the suffix ''-test.chp''.
  - Combine scans the config's directory. It skips the combine config itself, dot directories and bytecode files.

- Any function in global-scope, named ''Test*'' contained in a test file, is seen as a test.

*Running tests:*

When running one or multiple tests, combine resolves the dependency graph for each ''*-test.chp'' file, and then runs the ''Test*'' functions within the test files.

No test can leak state into other tests, all test functions run isolated from each other.

*Test results:*

A test PASSes only when it returned ''0'' or ''null'', for example: ''return 0;'' or ''return null;'' was called, or the program fell off the end. Anything else returned is interpreted as a FAIL and is printed in the test report.

*Reporting:*

The runner captures each test's ''STDOUT'' and ''STDERR'' outputs, and re-prints them in the test report under the corresponding test.

Only Output within the actual test runtime (''CHIPRT == 0'') is captured, outputs written from an ''actor(function, arg1, arg2, ...)'' is not captured.

Printing to ''STDOUT'' or ''STDERR'' in a test has no influence on if a test is interpreted as PASS or FAIL.

*Returns:*

- Exit code 0 when all tests PASSed
- Exit code 1 when at least one test FAILed

*Recommended Reading*

''chippy doc combine''
